sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-thompson-audit-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Thompson's Scarus -> Pomacanthus coordinate transformation fitted to real species — Model fidelity to source: 78/100" ;
        rdfs:comment "As before: \"coaxial circles\" formalised as the Moebius group with the reading stated, the oblique family added for Fig. 376 as drawn, the alternatives Thompson compares against (rectilinear coordinates) and does not (affine) fitted the same way, the thin-plate spline of Bookstein 1989 as the exact deformation, fitters checked on synthetic maps. Raised because the thing Thompson actually deformed - an outline - is now carried by each family and compared with a real outline, so curvature between the landmarks is no longer untested, and because the test is set up so that his family can only win by beating the no-deformation baseline, which is the comparison his sentence makes (\"rectilinear co-ordinates\" -> \"coaxial circles\" -> \"a very good outline\"). Not higher because his drawn grid is still displayed, not digitised and compared constant by constant; because the landmark test rests on genus means and the outline test on one individual per species, so neither is his \"typical Scaroid fish\"; and because the maps are fitted to the landmarks and only applied to the outline, so a map fitted to the outline itself (semilandmarks) is not tried. Evidence: thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py L5–L23: the claim quoted; the reading of coaxial circles as a Moebius map <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/232e8f8/thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py#L5-L23>; thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py L47–L83: what is computed: the five families, noise floor, context, LOO, and item 7, the real outlines <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/232e8f8/thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py#L47-L83>; thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py L228–L289: moebius()/fit_moebius()/coaxial()/fit_coaxial(): the two coaxial families <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/232e8f8/thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py#L228-L289>; thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py L290–L310: tps_fit()/tps_apply(): Bookstein 1989 with bending energy <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/232e8f8/thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py#L290-L310>; thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py L323–L333: self_test(): known maps recovered <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/232e8f8/thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py#L323-L333>; thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py L701–L738: outline_analysis(): maps fitted to the species' landmarks, applied to the Scarus silhouette, scored against the Pomacanthus silhouette <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/232e8f8/thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py#L701-L738>." ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-model-fidelity> ;
        pk:hasProbability "0.78"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-model-fidelity> rdfs:label "Thompson's Scarus -> Pomacanthus coordinate transformation fitted to real species (thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py) satisfies the MorphoEval 0.1.0 criterion 'Model fidelity to source' for Scarus (22 spp.) and Pomacanthus (9 spp.), with Chaetodon (54 spp.) and 59 other genera for context; one photographed S. ghobban and one P. semicirculatus; Indo-Pacific shore fishes, lateral view" ;
        dct:identifier "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Claude Fable 5.1 (Cursor agent)" .
}

